From 4bbc9708083ed642e215e872868c0e14e9ac2f0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the upscaler of the videos of this kind
 from a button of the Video page

The upscalers (RAVU, FSRCNNX) were only in Settings > Player > Videos, at
the level Expert, and could not be found from a video. The Video page of
the player information (O) now has a button under its column of the video
output, above the bar: it names the kind of the video that plays (1080p
and above, below 1080p, or animation where that has a setting of its own)
and the upscaler chosen for it. OK on it, or on the Video tab, opens a
list whose heading says that the choice is for every video of that kind,
as it is: it sets that setting of Player > Videos, which applies at once,
and kodi.log says what was set. Down from the tabs goes to it, and down
again to the button of the output of this video where that is shown: that
one stays in the bar, as on the other pages, and up from it comes back to
the button of the upscaler. No column of the page reaches the button
(tools/regress/playerinfo, skin_check). PlayerControl(HadesUpscaler) asks
for the same list from a keymap. The settings stay off by default.
